 "title": "Zero-drift bidirectional current-sense amplifier, INA181 and INA180",
 "source": {
  "document": "835-11-B5",
  "revision": "2024-08-A1",
  "pages": 12
 },
 "summary": "The INA181 and INA180 amplify the small voltage across a current shunt, in either direction, while the shunt sits anywhere from -0.2 V to 30 V of common mode; uses include battery monitoring, power management and overcurrent detection. A matched internal resistor network fixes the gain at 20, 50, 100 or 200 V/V. They run from one 2.7 V to 5.5 V supply with a rail-to-rail output. The INA181 in SOT23-6 brings out a REF pin; the INA180 in SOT23-5 references its output to ground and comes in two pinouts.",
