 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gain options",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Gain is set inside the part by a matched resistor network and is chosen by part number: option 1 gives 20 V/V, 2 gives 50 V/V, 3 gives 100 V/V and 4 gives 200 V/V. The INA181 comes in options A1 to A4; the INA180 in A1 to A4 and B1 to B4."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output reference",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Both devices are a difference amplifier with four internal resistors. In the INA181 the reference end of the network comes out on REF; the electrical characteristics are given with VREF = VS/2. In the INA180 that end is tied to ground inside the package."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply and bypass",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "The part needs a bypass capacitor on its supply for stable operation, placed close to the pins; the typical circuits use 0.1 µF."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Layout",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Run IN+ and IN- straight to the two ends of the shunt so that as little resistance as possible adds in series with it."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "The output swings rail to rail: within 30 mV of VS and within 5 mV of ground into 10 kΩ, and is stable with up to 1 nF of load capacitance."
  }
 ],
